# ThinkPink packaging license (staging copy for the fresh public repo)

## The short version

ThinkPink is free for everyone. Use it, share it, rebuild it, learn
from it. Nobody sells this exact packaging; if you want to sell
something, build your own.

## The license

The ThinkPink packaging layer (the governance modules, the reskin, and
the desktop wrapper built by the Stardust Lab) is released under

    CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

That means, in plain terms:

- **BY (Attribution).** Credit where it came from.
- **NC (NonCommercial).** Commercial use is excluded. Nobody may sell
  this packaging or charge for it.
- **SA (ShareAlike).** Anything built from this packaging carries the
  same terms: free and noncommercial, all the way down.

Copyright for the ThinkPink packaging layer: The ThinkPink builders.

## What this license does NOT cover

- **Hindsight** (github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight, by Vectorize AI,
  Inc.) is MIT licensed and remains under its own license, untouched
  and credited. Their MIT is what makes this build possible.
- The vellum-assistant shell and the lab's other open tools carry
  their own licenses (MIT), stated in their own repositories.

## The spirit clause

This project exists because the people who built it chose not to
profit from it. The license enforces the letter. The hope, stated
plainly: if you build on this, build on your own thinking, and keep
what you make free.
